About Nebius:

Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.

Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.

Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.

The role &nbsp;

Nebius is scaling our Digital Native sales team to bring AI-native GPU infrastructure to the fastest-moving builders in the AI economy.&nbsp;You’ll&nbsp;join a segment-aligned go-to-market motion focused on Digital Native Businesses (DNB), Independent Software Vendors (ISVs), and Gaming customers, and establish&nbsp;Nebius&nbsp;as the AI infrastructure platform of choice for companies whose product is software. &nbsp;

We’re&nbsp;seeking experienced Account Executives with&nbsp;a track record&nbsp;of selling cloud infrastructure, GPUs, or AI/ML platforms into digital native, ISV, and gaming organizations. You will own a named account list within one or more of these segments, drive multi-year AI infrastructure commitments, and operationalize a partner-led GTM model anchored in NVIDIA, ecosystem software partners, and strategic SIs. This is a high-impact sales role for reps who can pair technical fluency with fast, founder- and engineering-led deal execution. &nbsp;

You are welcome to work remotely from the US. SF, NYC, Boston, or Seattle preferred- Travel as&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;customer, partner, and industry events. &nbsp;

Your responsibilities will include: &nbsp;

• Own the Full Sales Cycle:&nbsp; Manage complex, multi-stakeholder deals from prospecting to close across named DNB, ISV, and Gaming accounts. &nbsp;

• Drive Segment-Specific GPU Adoption:&nbsp; Translate&nbsp;Nebius’s&nbsp;NVIDIA-based GPU platform (H100, H200, B200, GB200 NVL72, and beyond) into use cases - model training, fine-tuning, inference at scale, RAG,&nbsp;MLOps, rendering and simulation - that map to product and unit-economics outcomes. &nbsp;

• Sell to Technical Buyers:&nbsp; Multi-thread across founders, CTOs, VPs of Engineering, Heads of AI/ML, Infrastructure and Platform leads, and finance stakeholders who own compute spend. &nbsp;

• Move at Digital Native Speed:&nbsp; Run compressed, technically rigorous evaluations - benchmarks, POCs, and capacity trials - and convert them into committed consumption. &nbsp;

• Co-Sell with Partners:&nbsp; Run joint account plans with NVIDIA, ecosystem software partners, and SIs; structure co-sell motions that combine GPU infrastructure, software ecosystem, and services. &nbsp;

• Forecast &amp; Execute:&nbsp; Maintain&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;pipeline management and deliver predictable results against quota. &nbsp;

• Land &amp; Expand:&nbsp; Drive multi-year expansion across AI training, inference, and&nbsp;production&nbsp;AI workloads within named accounts as their usage scales. &nbsp;

• Market Intelligence:&nbsp; Stay ahead of AI model and tooling trends, GPU market dynamics, and competitive moves across the digital native, ISV, and gaming landscape to position Nebius effectively. &nbsp;

We expect you to have: &nbsp;

• 8+ years of B2B sales experience in AI infrastructure, GPUs, cloud&nbsp;compute, or enterprise platforms. &nbsp;

• Proven success closing complex infrastructure or platform deals within digital native, ISV, or gaming accounts. &nbsp;

• Strong understanding of how software-first companies evaluate, buy, and scale compute, including consumption-based commercial models. &nbsp;

